WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.339
"Zann! Stop!"

2
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.208
A sudden blast of energy grabbed Zann's body, flinging him back.

3
00:00:18.209 --> 00:00:21.962
He landed hard on the ground, several yards from the wormhole.

4
00:00:21.963 --> 00:00:25.035
When he looked up, the wormhole was spinning shut.

5
00:00:25.036 --> 00:00:30.800
A moment later Boz was hauling him up by the arm. The old man's face was livid.

6
00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:39.142
"What were you thinking?" Boz shouted, his long nose quivering with rage. "Have you gone mad, boy?"

7
00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:42.895
"How did you—" Zann didn't get a chance to finish the question.

8
00:00:42.896 --> 00:00:46.268
Boz snapped his fingers and zapped them both away.

9
00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:53.719
They landed in Teplo's living room. "You got him in time!" Gliss cried. "Thank goodness!"

10
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:58.225
Zann ducked as Zing flew at him, blasting him with angry flames.

11
00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:06.817
"Quit it," Zann muttered. Glancing around, he saw Perda, Darb, and Teplo staring at him. "What's going on?"

12
00:01:06.818 --> 00:01:10.363
"Zing woke up and realized you were gone," Darb said.

13
00:01:10.364 --> 00:01:12.918
"He freaked out and rushed to find me."

14
00:01:12.919 --> 00:01:17.638
Zann scowled at the dragon. Then he realized what Darb had said.

15
00:01:17.639 --> 00:01:23.775
"Wait," said Zann. "What do you mean, he rushed to find you? You were in the same room."

16
00:01:23.776 --> 00:01:30.942
"Not exactly." Darb's face went red. "Um, I promised Gliss I'd meet her after midnight.

17
00:01:30.943 --> 00:01:34.778
I guess I didn't notice you were gone when I woke up and sneaked out."

18
00:01:34.779 --> 00:01:37.832
Zann looked at Gliss. She was blushing too.

19
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:43.895
"I had something important to tell him," she said. "I'm leaving First City tomorrow."

20
00:01:43.896 --> 00:01:47.983
Zann just shrugged, thinking of what he'd overheard earlier.

21
00:01:47.984 --> 00:01:52.243
He wasn't surprised that Gliss was leaving for Swamp Bottom tomorrow too.

22
00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:56.191
Her parents and her uncle had been involved in the same meetings as Boz.

23
00:01:56.192 --> 00:01:59.245
"Whatever you say," he said with a smirk.

24
00:01:59.246 --> 00:02:05.858
"I think Darb would have figured out you'd left First City when he saw you in Swamp Bottom tomorrow with the rest of us."

25
00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.966
"Huh?" Darb looked confused. "No, you don't understand.

26
00:02:09.967 --> 00:02:12.505
Gliss isn't going back to Swamp Bottom.

27
00:02:12.506 --> 00:02:16.251
She's going on an expedition to the Cave of the Unknown."

28
00:02:16.252 --> 00:02:21.991
"What?" Zann whirled toward Gliss. "The Cave of the Unknown," he repeated.

29
00:02:21.992 --> 00:02:25.500
"Are you serious? Why are you going there?"

30
00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:29.181
The Cave of the Unknown was a remote and dangerous place.

31
00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:33.863
Few people had seen it, and even fewer had survived to describe it.

32
00:02:33.864 --> 00:02:41.758
Zann's parents were among those few. They had visited the Cave a couple of times, returning with many frightening stories about it.

33
00:02:41.759 --> 00:02:47.216
Staring at the floor, Gliss shrugged. "My parents are making me go."

34
00:02:47.217 --> 00:02:52.833
Zann hardly heard her. He was still thinking about all the stories he'd heard during his childhood.

35
00:02:52.834 --> 00:03:01.387
"My parents said the Cave of the Unknown is huge and really spooky, with countless tunnels and chambers," he said.

36
00:03:01.388 --> 00:03:07.466
"The whole place is littered with ancient relics and manuscripts from the Old Times and stuff."

37
00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:13.940
"Yeah. Like the relics and texts Morb used to try to take over Magica," Perda said with a shudder.

38
00:03:13.941 --> 00:03:20.760
"Exactly. That's why the Red Council decided it's time to seal the place off," Teplo put in.

39
00:03:20.761 --> 00:03:25.800
"Until now they've relied on the Cave's reputation to keep people away.

40
00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:32.753
But after Morb's recent adventures, they don't want anyone else coming along and trying the same thing.

41
00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:37.857
The Council is sending an expedition to seal it off so the relics can't be removed."

42
00:03:37.858 --> 00:03:41.293
Boz didn't seem to be paying much attention to the conversation.

43
00:03:41.294 --> 00:03:45.578
His nose quivering wildly, he was still glaring at Zann.

44
00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:50.536
Zann recognized that look. It meant his grandfather was thinking hard.

45
00:03:50.537 --> 00:03:55.391
He was probably trying to come up with the perfect way to punish Zann for sneaking out tonight.

46
00:03:55.392 --> 00:03:59.523
Boz spoke out at last. "Enough about the expedition.

47
00:03:59.524 --> 00:04:03.606
We were discussing Zann's outrageous behavior."

48
00:04:03.607 --> 00:04:06.621
Zann cringed. Then he looked over at Darb.

49
00:04:06.622 --> 00:04:11.300
"So you saw I was missing and ran to tell Boz?" he asked.

50
00:04:11.301 --> 00:04:15.029
"I never thought you were the type to tell on your friends."

51
00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:18.200
"That's not what happened," Gliss said.

52
00:04:18.201 --> 00:04:22.525
"When Darb and I realized you were missing, we checked with Perda.

53
00:04:22.526 --> 00:04:29.272
She didn't know where you were, but she tried all your passwords and was eventually able to make your note appear."

54
00:04:29.273 --> 00:04:33.870
"I can't believe you didn't tell me you were going, Zann," Perda added.

55
00:04:33.871 --> 00:04:38.373
Her eyes flashed with anger, and her voice was cool and unfriendly.

56
00:04:38.374 --> 00:04:41.178
Zann hated having her look at him that way.

57
00:04:41.179 --> 00:04:46.226
He wished he could make her understand why he'd tried to go through the wormhole without telling his friends.

58
00:04:46.227 --> 00:04:48.679
But he wasn't sure how to communicate that.

59
00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.935
"Gliss came to us right away, thank goodness," Teplo said.

60
00:04:52.936 --> 00:04:59.656
"Since we knew you wouldn't be able to reach the palace wormhole, Boz guessed you might try the one in Wormwood."

61
00:04:59.657 --> 00:05:05.432
Zann glared at Gliss. "You ratted me out? I thought we were friends!"

62
00:05:05.433 --> 00:05:10.737
"We are," Gliss said, looking hurt. "I was trying to help you."

63
00:05:10.738 --> 00:05:14.979
"Help me?" Zann gritted his teeth, furious.

64
00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.918
"I helped you to reunite with your parents, remember?

65
00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:22.858
All you did tonight was stop me from doing the same thing!"

66
00:05:22.859 --> 00:05:27.568
"No," Darb said. "She stopped you from disappearing forever."

67
00:05:27.569 --> 00:05:32.536
"That's right, Zann." Boz sounded disapproving. He glanced at Teplo.

68
00:05:32.537 --> 00:05:38.047
"I'm starting to think it's a mistake to let Zann come along when we leave tomorrow."

69
00:05:38.048 --> 00:05:41.692
"You mean you might not take me back to Swamp Bottom?"

70
00:05:41.693 --> 00:05:45.917
Zann rolled his eyes. That didn't sound like much of a punishment to him.

71
00:05:45.918 --> 00:05:50.920
"Swamp Bottom? Who's going to Swamp Bottom?" Boz asked.

72
00:05:50.921 --> 00:05:58.731
"We are," Zann said. "I heard you two talking about it earlier. You said we leave tomorrow afternoon."

73
00:05:58.732 --> 00:06:03.078
"Yes, we do," Teplo said. "But not for Swamp Bottom.

74
00:06:03.079 --> 00:06:07.373
Your grandfather and I are part of the expedition Gliss mentioned.

75
00:06:07.374 --> 00:06:09.692
That means you're part of it too."

76
00:06:09.693 --> 00:06:19.597
Boz nodded. "That's right, Zann. You're going to the Cave of the Unknown."
